    "result_text": "The sheet's due-total and overdue-total are now trimmed, and all 4 acceptance tests pass with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**The rule:** when three or more people have a figure, both sheet totals leave out the single highest and the single lowest person's figure. A person whose due-total is n/a has no figure, so they don't count towards the three. Every person always has an overdue figure, even when it is 0.00.\n\nThe rule is applied in two places that work out the totals separately, so they stay in step:\n\n- **Server** (`RollupService.java`): the totals are now worked out this way, so the TOTALS lines in the audit file use the trimmed figures.\n- **Front end** (`people.ts`): the totals row and the header show the same trimmed figures.\n\nNothing else is trimmed: per-person figures, the overdue count, per-grade and per-period totals, backing and the claimed total add up as before. No change to the stored data was needed.",
